    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nI've been thinking of integrating mini.diff  into [aider.nvim](https://github.com/awei89/aider.nvim), and using to show the user the AI generated code changes.\n\nI'm able to run `MiniDiff.set_ref_text` prior to the AI generated changes being applied. But ideally I'd like to freeze the diff once the changes have been applied so that if the user adds additional text, it's not included in the diff being shown. Running `disable` stops showing the diff entirely. But I'm wondering if it might be possible to stop tracking new changes as part of the diff but keep the prior diff in-place\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-01-26T12:20:51Z",
